parts.latex:
The diagram below is a scale drawing of a block of land. The scale used is $1:2000$.

\exfigure{496_q24_1}

By measurement, calculate the actual perimeter of the block of land in kilometres.

solutions.latex:
The lake is split into two strips of width $30$ m, with the parallel sides read from the map. Using the trapezoidal rule on each strip, $A = \dfrac{h}{2}(a+b)$:

\exfigure{3303_q10_s1}
$$\begin{aligned} A &= A_1 + A_2 \\ &= \dfrac{30}{2}(30+20) + \dfrac{30}{2}(20+0) \\ &= 750 + 300 \\ &= 1050 \text{ m}^2 \end{aligned}$$

